      {
        "id": 213848,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-05T21:16:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There are some abilities that specifically say a bonus or penalty is \"destroyed,\" but I agree, the terminology is neither consistent nor well-defined.&nbsp; In <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/boosthinder-questions-11162\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">another thread</a>, I speculated it meant \"by other abilities that say \"destroy\" and not being consumed or canceled by an opposite penalty or bonus,\" and Dave replied but didn't correct me, so I'm going with that.</p><p>I came up with another couple of questions, though.</p><p>The first is with when you make selections (again).&nbsp; For instance, for Hasty Augmentation, do you decide whether to use Max or Mid+Persistent before or after rolling?&nbsp; For Brainstorm, do you decide which target to attack with Min and which with Mid before or after rolling?&nbsp; I'm guessing it's all before--it seems like all decisions need to be made before--but it's not clear.</p><p>Second, it was confirmed that \"your\" in Volatile Parts means \"that you created.\"&nbsp; Is that true for other heroes as well?&nbsp; For instance, if Unity uses Hasty Augmentation to soup up one of Wraith's knives, can Wraith use that bonus for Unleash?&nbsp; If Bunker boosts another hero, would he destroy that boost when using Omni-Blast?</p><p>And that just made me think of another: If Unity creates a Boost for another hero, and then that hero is separated from Unity and that bonus is then destroyed, does it explode?&nbsp; If it does explode, does Unity's player choose the target even though she has no idea what's going on?&nbsp; Similarly, what happens if Bunker boosts a hero that then gets separated from him, and he uses Satellite Recall or Omni-Blast?</p><p>...Aaand looking at this stuff for Bunker, yet another: Emergency Reconfiguration says \"you take extra damage equal to the Min die.\"&nbsp; What Min die?&nbsp; Bunker isn't rolling anything.&nbsp; You don't even get a Min die on reactions (they use only one die).&nbsp; If he's being attacked by a minion or a lieutenant (which is usually--in the whole starter kit there are only two enemies that roll multiple dice and you're not supposed to fight one of them), there's no Min die there either.</p>",
