      {
        "id": 213849,
        "name": "Chilly Steke",
        "username": "Chilly_Steke",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chilly_steke/{size}/1965_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-05T23:20:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If Unity creates a Boost for another hero, and then that hero is separated from Unity and that bonus is then destroyed, does it explode?&nbsp; If it does explode, does Unity's player choose the target even though she has no idea what's going on?&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This is the only one of your questions I feel qualified to answer-- The way I feel like Volatile Parts is supposed to work narratively is that she is making things out of metal that are unstable and explosive, so if some metal boost she made is destroyed then it should definitely explode. So narratively, if she's around, she can choose the target when it explodes, but if she isn't around, perhaps it explodes but without so much precision— more collateral damage? That's my thought from a narrative perspective if not with an exact mechanistic exactitude.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
